From a62d892c0c11d64c84279ec69f1accf218688719 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mat Kowalski <mko@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 22:54:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] CNO: declare VIP prefixes on the router and avoid
 masters by role

The frr-k8s validation webhook requires advertised prefixes to be
declared at router level. The DaemonSet now avoids control plane nodes
by role whenever BGP VIP management is active: label-based
anti-affinity raced DaemonSet scheduling and NodeRestriction denies
the static pod's node labeling anyway.

Found during the first end-to-end BGP VIP install.
